---
import Resumen from "../../layouts/Resumen.astro";
import {
  LABELLED_AXES,
  REGION_HEADING,
} from "../../lib/subscriber/labels.ts";
import {
  DEFAULT_SUBSCRIBER_LOCALE,
  MAX_SUBSCRIPTIONS_PER_SUBSCRIBER,
} from "../../lib/subscriber/policy.ts";
import { MAX_REGION_LENGTH } from "@pawster/domain";

/**
 * Save a search.
 *
 * **Prerendered, and it has to be.** ADR 0007's rule is that the Worker runs as rarely as
 * possible, and this is the page every link to Pawster's digest points at — a server-rendered
 * one would spend an invocation per visit to show a form that never varies. It is also the
 * cheapest way to satisfy the identical-response rule: a static form renders nothing about the
 * address it is given, so there is no server-side branch here to get wrong.
 *
 * The checkboxes are generated from `domain/`'s vocabularies through `labels.ts`, so an axis
 * value added there appears here without an edit — and cannot appear without a Spanish word,
 * because the label records are `satisfies Record<...>` and a missing one fails the build.
 *
 * The one axis rendered as free text is region, and ADR 0005 is why: the vocabulary is
 * per-country reference data rather than a union this repository closes, so there is no list
 * to offer until #56's filter panel has the data behind it.
 */
---

<Resumen
  title="Recibe el resumen"
  heading="Recibe animales en adopción por correo"
  indexable={true}
>
  <p>
    Dinos qué estás buscando y te mandamos un resumen por correo, una vez por semana, con los
    animales que aparecieron y te calzan. Sin cuenta y sin contraseña.
  </p>

  <form method="post" action="/api/resumen/suscribir">
    <p>
      <label for="email">Tu correo</label><br />
      <input
        id="email"
        name="email"
        type="email"
        required
        maxlength="200"
        autocomplete="email"
      />
    </p>

    {
      LABELLED_AXES.map((axis) => (
        <fieldset>
          <legend>{axis.heading}</legend>
          {axis.values.map((item) => (
            <p>
              <label>
                <input type="checkbox" name={axis.field} value={item.value} />
                {item.label}
              </label>
            </p>
          ))}
        </fieldset>
      ))
    }

    <fieldset>
      <legend>{REGION_HEADING}</legend>
      <p>
        <label for="regions">Estados, separados por comas</label><br />
        <input
          id="regions"
          name="regions"
          type="text"
          maxlength={MAX_REGION_LENGTH * 4}
          placeholder="Miranda, Distrito Capital, Aragua"
        />
      </p>
      <p>
        <!--
          Named as the reason it is a text box rather than a list, because a subscriber typing
          a state that matches nothing gets silence and would otherwise have no way to guess
          why. ADR 0005: a typo in a region matches no animal instead of failing to save.
        -->
        Escríbelos como se llaman. Si escribes uno que no existe, simplemente no te va a
        calzar ningún animal.
      </p>
    </fieldset>

    <!--
      The locale the subscriber is reading in, carried so it can be stored with them: the
      resumen is the one thing Pawster sends that has no URL to read a language off (ADR 0018).
      A hidden field the platform's own page sets, never anything the visitor chooses, which is
      why `parseLocale()` falls back instead of refusing.
    -->
    <input type="hidden" name="locale" value={DEFAULT_SUBSCRIBER_LOCALE} />

    <p data-testid="everything-notice">
      Si no marcas nada, te mandamos <strong>todos</strong> los animales que aparezcan.
    </p>

    <p><button type="submit">Mándame el resumen</button></p>
  </form>

  <p data-testid="opt-in-notice">
    <!--
      That the first mail is a link to activate, said before it arrives. An adopter who
      expects animals and receives one line with a link is an adopter who reports it as spam,
      and a complaint costs a Do-Not-Contact entry that outlives everything else we hold
      (ADR 0010).
    -->
    Te va a llegar un correo con un enlace para activarla. Hasta que lo abras no te mandamos
    nada más: así nadie puede anotar el correo de otra persona.
  </p>

  <p>
    Puedes guardar hasta {MAX_SUBSCRIPTIONS_PER_SUBSCRIBER} búsquedas distintas con el mismo
    correo, y llegan todas en el mismo resumen.
  </p>
</Resumen>
